.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
adds,
edits or removes dependency information in a bundle’s
.Sy info file .
This command does not install dependencies;
that is the responsibility of
.Xr jeep-prep 1 .
.Pp
Each operation is a subcommand.
The
.Fl "-vendor"
option applies to whichever subcommand is used and so is given
before the subcommand’s name.
.
.Ss Options
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Xo
.Fl v ,
.Fl "-vendor"
.Xc
Operates on the dependencies that will be vendored rather than
the dependencies that will be installed to the
.Sy syspath .
Vendoring is discussed below in
.Sx "Vendoring" .
.El
.
.Ss Subcommands
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Xo
.Ic add
.Oo
.Fl a No \&|
.Fl "-autotag"
.Oc
.Ar deps
.No ...
.Xc
Adds one or more dependencies to the bundle’s
.Sy info file .
Each dependency can be specified by a URL or a JDN struct/table.
A struct/table must contain the
.Ql ":name"
and
.Ql ":url"
keys and the
.Ql ":name"
must be a string.
A dependency that cannot be resolved to a URL is an error.
A dependency that is already listed is skipped.
.It Xo
.Ic edit
.Oo
.Fl a No \&|
.Fl "-autotag"
.Oc
.Ar dep
.Oo
.Ar key
.Ar value
.Oc
.No ...
.Xc
Edits a single dependency in the bundle’s
.Sy info file .
The dependency can be specified by its name or its URL and must
already be listed.
.Pp
Each
.Ar key
is a keyword.
Each pair is set on the dependency:
a
.Ar key
that is already present has its
.Ar value
replaced and a
.Ar key
that is absent is added.
Keys that are not named are left untouched and a
.Ar value
of
.Ql "nil"
removes the
.Ar key .
If the dependency is listed as a bare name,
it is converted into a struct.
.Pp
A dependency is found by its
.Ql ":name" ,
so that key must be a string,
cannot be removed and cannot be given the name of another listed
dependency.
The dependency can otherwise be renamed freely.
No pair is applied if any pair in the same invocation breaks
one of these rules.
.Pp
A
.Ar value
is read as a JDN value only if it reads whole and is not a symbol.
Anything else is taken as a string,
so a URL,
a path or a tag needs no quoting beyond what the shell requires.
A
.Ar value
that should be a string despite looking like a number or a boolean
must be quoted,
as described in
.Sx "Values"
in
.Xr jeep-meta 1 .
.It Xo
.Ic rem
.Ar deps
.No ...
.Xc
Removes one or more dependencies from the bundle’s
.Sy info file .
Each dependency can be specified by its name or its URL.
.It Xo
.Ic tidy
.Xc
Sorts the bundle’s dependencies by name.
Comments and blank lines in the
.Sy info file
are preserved.
.El
.Pp
The
.Fl "-autotag"
option,
available on
.Ic add
and
.Ic edit ,
sets the
.Ql ":tag"
key of each dependency to the SHA of the current commit of the
dependency’s repository.
The dependency must have a
.Ql ":url"
key for this to be possible.
.
.Ss Vendoring
A bundle’s
.Sy info file
can contain dependency information in an array/tuple mapped
to the
.Ql ":dependencies"
key.
By default,
dependencies that are added,
edited or removed using
.Nm
are added to,
edited in or removed from this data structure.
Dependencies that are listed in this data structure are installed
into the
.Sy syspath .
This will either be the global syspath or
.Eo
.Pa ./_system
.Ec ,
the local syspath,
if the user is using the
.Fl "-local"
flag as described in
.Xr jeep 1 .
.Pp
Janet does not support the installation of multiple versions
of a dependency.
To avoid version conflicts,
a user may prefer to vendor dependencies.
.Nm
supports this with the
.Fl "-vendor"
option.
Vendored dependencies are listed in an array/tuple under the
.Ql ":vendored"
keyword.
.Pp
A vendored dependency is similar to an ordinary dependency.
That is,
it is a struct/table containing the
.Ql ":name"
and
.Ql ":url"
keys.
It can also include the
.Ql ":tag" ,
.Ql ":prefix" ,
and
.Ql ":paths"
keys.
If the
.Ql ":paths"
key is present,
a vendored dependency will be fetched from the specified URL
and the values used to copy files into the bundle.
If the values are strings,
the relative path of the source file matches the relative path
of the destination file.
However,
if the value is a two-element array/tuple,
the file located at the path in the first value will be copied
to the path in the second value.
See
.Sx "EXAMPLES"
below.
.Pp
For more information about the
.Sy info file ,
the
.Sy bundle script
and the
.Sy syspath ,
see CONCEPTS in
.Xr jeep 1 .
.
.Sh EXAMPLES
To add a dependency to the
.Sy info file :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ jeep dep add https://example\&.org/foo\&.git
.Ed
.Pp
To edit a dependency in the
.Sy info file
so it has the SHA of the current commit:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ jeep dep edit -a foo
.Ed
.Pp
To remove a dependency from the
.Sy info file :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ jeep dep rem foo
.Ed
.Pp
To sort the dependencies in the
.Sy info file
by name:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ jeep dep tidy
.Ed
.Pp
To add two dependencies that will be vendored:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ jeep dep -v add https://example\&.org/foo\&.git https://example\&.org/bar\&.git
.Ed
.Pp
To add a vendored dependency that will selectively copy files:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ jeep dep -v add \(aq{:name \(dqfoo\(dq \e
                    :url \(dqhttps://example\&.org/foo\(dq \e
                    :prefix \(dqdeps\(dq \e
                    :paths \(lB\(lB\(dqa\&.janet\(dq \(dqb\&.janet\(dq\(rB \e
                            \(lB\(dqc\&.janet\(dq \(dqc/init\&.janet\(dq\(rB\(rB}\(aq
.Ed
.Pp
To set a key on a vendored dependency:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ jeep dep -v edit foo :prefix \(aq\(dqdeps/foo\(dq\(aq
.Ed
.Pp
To remove a key from a vendored dependency:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ jeep dep -v edit foo :prefix nil
.Ed
.
